# Run the API first (see README "Local setup"), then send these top to bottom.
# Requests share variables, so each step uses the order created in step 1.
# Seeded ids: customer bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-8000-000000000001,
#             products aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-00000000000{1,2,3} (stock 15 / 50 / 5).

@OrderManagement.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5196

### 0. Liveness
GET {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/health

### 1. Create an order -> 201 + Location. Idempotency-Key is REQUIRED (1-256 chars).
# @name createOrder
POST {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-create-1
X-Correlation-Id: demo-trace-1

{
  "customerId": "bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
  "shippingAddress": "Jl. Sudirman 1",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-000000000002", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### 1b. Same key + same body again -> the same 201 (replay, stock deducted once).
###     Change the body but keep the key -> 422 business_rule.

@orderId = {{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Get the order -> 200 (unknown id -> 404 not_found)
GET {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 3. List orders -> { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }
###    Filters: status, customerId, from, to (ISO 8601). page>=1, pageSize 1-100.
GET {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders?status=Pending&page=1&pageSize=20

### 4. Confirm: Pending -> Confirmed -> Shipped -> Delivered (illegal jump -> 422)
PATCH {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Confirmed" }

### 5. Cancel (Pending/Confirmed only; restores stock) -> 200, again -> 409
POST {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel

### Error examples (all return application/problem+json with a `code`)

### E1. Missing Idempotency-Key -> 400 validation
POST {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-8000-000000000001", "shippingAddress": "x",
  "items": [ { "productId": "aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-000000000002", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### E2. Several invalid fields -> 400 validation with per-field `errors`
POST {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-1

{ "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "shippingAddress": "",
  "items": [ { "productId": "aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-000000000002", "quantity": 0 } ] }

### E3. Insufficient stock (product 3 has 5) -> 409 conflict
POST {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-stock-1

{ "customerId": "bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-8000-000000000001", "shippingAddress": "Jl. Sudirman 1",
  "items": [ { "productId": "aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-8000-000000000003", "quantity": 6 } ] }

### E4. Unknown status name -> 400 validation listing the allowed values
PATCH {{OrderManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Bogus" }
